TEXT 96 48 Left 3 ;#406 Differential amplifier with a current-regulator tail
TEXT 96 112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VXZH3UE-kSw
TEXT 96 160 Left 2 ;A current regulator diode sets the pair's bias current, so the gain holds as the common mode moves.
TEXT 96 920 Left 2 ;The three VCM_VAL steps are the common-mode settings Alan reads on his meter, and 5 kHz is his
TEXT 96 952 Left 2 ;generator frequency. Vsig is 1 V AC, so V(OUT_L,OUT_R) in dB is the differential gain directly.
TEXT 96 1008 Left 2 !.step param VCM_VAL list 3.54 4.05 5.61
TEXT 96 1048 Left 2 !.ac dec 100 10 1Meg
TEXT 96 1088 Left 2 !.include ..\..\..\LTspice\Models\Unverified\1N5297_illustrative.lib
TEXT 700 1048 Left 2 ;Alan does not name the tail diode, so the 1 mA 1N5297 model is an explicit modeling choice.
TEXT 700 1008 Left 2 !.meas ac GAIN_5K FIND mag(V(OUT_L,OUT_R)/V(IN)) AT=5k
